# Authentication Flow – Password Recovery Test Execution Report

## Test Case

Test Case: Password Recovery Using a Registered Email Address
Use Case: Password Recovery
Test Type: Automated End-to-End (E2E) Testing
Testing Tool: Cypress
Browser: Google Chrome
Application: Student Survey Application
Application URL: https://student.michaelkentburns.com/
Test File: cypress/e2e/david/password-recovery.cy.js
Final Status: PASS

## Context

This test was performed to validate the Password Recovery functionality of the Student Survey Application. The objective was to ensure that users who forget their password can securely request a password reset using their registered email address.

During the test, the complete password recovery workflow was executed, starting from accessing the recovery page to submitting a password reset request. The application was also verified to ensure it provided the appropriate confirmation message after the request was successfully processed.

In addition, an extra validation was performed using an email address that was not registered in the system to confirm that the application correctly prevents unauthorized password recovery attempts by displaying an appropriate error message.

## Preconditions

### Before executing the test, the following conditions were met:

Cypress was successfully installed and configured.
The Student Survey Application was available.
A valid registered user account existed.
The Password Recovery page was accessible.
The application was connected to the authentication system.

### Test Scenario :

The automated test covered the following workflow:

Open the Student Survey Application.
Open the User menu.
Navigate to the Login page.
Open the Lost your password? page.
Enter a registered email address.
Submit the password recovery request.
Verify that the application confirms the request.
Verify that the user is instructed to check their email.
 
