## Cypress Test Flow

describe('Password Recovery Test', () => {

  it('should recover password using a registered email address', () => {

    cy.visit('https://student.michaelkentburns.com/');

    cy.contains('User').click();

    cy.contains('Login').click();

    cy.contains('Lost your password?').click();

    cy.get('#user_login').type('mumemekaleba@gmail.com');

    cy.get('#wp-submit').click();

  });

});

##  Conclusion

The Password Recovery use case was successfully automated using Cypress. The application correctly guided the user through the password recovery process by allowing access to the recovery page, accepting a registered email address, processing the request, and displaying the appropriate confirmation message.

Additional validation also confirmed that the application correctly handled an unregistered email address by preventing the request and displaying an appropriate error message.

All executed test scenarios completed successfully, and the application behaved according to the expected requirements defined in the Password Recovery use case.

